menu "Display Service"

    config DISPLAY_SERVICE_FORCE_FULL_REFRESH
        bool "Force full-frame refresh (for panels without row addressing)"
        default n
        help
            Switch the LVGL display to LV_DISPLAY_RENDER_MODE_FULL after it has
            been registered with esp_lv_adapter, so LVGL invalidates and flushes
            the whole screen every frame instead of dirty rectangles.

            Required for display controllers whose driver cannot set a row
            address window, e.g. AXS15231B in QSPI mode. That driver skips the
            RASET (0x2B) command and streams pixels with RAMWR (0x2C) followed
            by RAMWRC (0x3C) continuations, which is only correct for
            contiguous bands starting at row 0. Under PARTIAL refresh the first
            frame (a full-screen invalidate) looks right and every subsequent
            partial update corrupts the image.

            The render mode cannot be requested through the adapter config:
            display_manager_pick_render_mode() keys off tear_avoid_mode, and
            display_manager_validate_tearing_mode() rejects every full-frame
            tear mode on PANEL_IF_OTHER (SPI/I2C). So this option allocates two
            full-frame draw buffers in PSRAM and installs them with
            lv_display_set_buffers() once registration has succeeded.

            Costs two full frames of PSRAM and makes every frame a full-screen
            transfer, so expect a lower frame rate.

    config DISPLAY_SERVICE_SKIP_PANEL_DISPON_DIRECT
        bool "Do NOT send DISPON (0x29) directly to the panel IO"
        default n
        help
            Display service normally pushes DISPON (0x29) straight to the panel
            IO handle after the board manager hands over the panel. Set this
            option to fall back to esp_lcd_panel_disp_on_off(panel, true).

            Some panel drivers register an inverted disp_on_off() callback.
            esp_lcd_panel_disp_on_off(panel, on_off) forwards on_off straight to
            panel->disp_on_off(), but the AXS15231B driver declares its handler
            as disp_off(panel, bool off) and maps off==true to DISPOFF (0x28).
            The mapping is inverted relative to the framework contract, so
            asking to turn the display ON actually sends 0x28 and the panel
            blanks - while the backlight stays lit.

            Every known-good AXS15231B integration works around this by passing
            false (Waveshare esp_bsp bsp_display.c, the hello_35b bring-up and
            xiaozhi-esp32 custom_lcd_display.cc all do it), which through the
            inversion emits the intended 0x29. Relying on that is fragile, so
            display service builds the 32-bit QSPI command itself and pushes
            DISPON (0x29) through esp_lcd_panel_io_tx_param() instead.

            The direct write is enabled by default because DISPON is idempotent:
            on a correctly implemented driver it merely duplicates the DISPON
            already sent during panel init. Only set this symbol if a specific
            panel misbehaves with the extra command.

endmenu
